          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "8.3 Some Problems Involving Fractions"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.109,
            0.189,
            0.846,
            0.243
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "？ "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Example 3:",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Leena made 5 cups of tea. She used "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\frac { 1 } { 4 }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " litre of milk for this. How much milk is there in each cup of tea?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.191,
            0.27,
            0.793,
            0.395
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "image_body",
              "index": 4,
              "bbox": [
                0.191,
                0.27,
                0.793,
                0.395
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_17_image_4.jpg",
              "content": ""
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.418,
            0.848,
            0.474
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Leena used "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\frac { 1 } { 4 }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " litres of milk in 5 cups of tea. So, in 1 cup of tea the volume of milk should be:"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.469,
            0.483,
            0.528,
            0.519
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_17_equation_6.jpg",
          "content": "\\frac{1}{4} \\div 5."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.521,
            0.548,
            0.543
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Writing this as multiplication, we have:"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.388,
            0.554,
            0.608,
            0.588
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_17_equation_8.jpg",
          "content": "5 \\times ( \\mathrm{mink} \\mathrm{per} \\mathrm{cap} ) = \\frac{1}{4}."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.591,
            0.807,
            0.612
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "We perform the division as follows as per Brahmagupta’s method:"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.614,
            0.512,
            0.646
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "The reciprocal of 5 (the divisor) is "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\frac{1}{5},"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.643,
            0.698,
            0.674
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Multiplying this reciprocal by the dividend "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "( \\frac { 1 } { 4 } ) ,"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " , we get"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.446,
            0.68,
            0.552,
            0.717
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_17_equation_12.jpg",
          "content": "\\frac { 1 } { 5 } \\times \\frac { 1 } { 4 } = \\frac { 1 } { 2 0 } ."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.174,
            0.716,
            0.559,
            0.751
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "So, each cup of tea has "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\frac { 1 } { 2 0 }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " litre of milk."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 14,
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.763,
            0.848,
            0.822
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Example 4:",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Some of the oldest examples of working with non-unit fractions occur in humanity’s oldest geometry texts, the Śhulbasūtra. Here is an example from Baudhāyana’s Śhulbasūtra (c. 800 BCE)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 15,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.828,
            0.848,
            0.889
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Cover an area of 7 "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\frac { 1 } { 2 }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " square units with square bricks each of whose sides is "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\frac { 1 } { 5 }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " units."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "page_number",
          "index": 16,
